v2-bootstrap: three documentation corrections on the reuse controls (PATCH 6)

Comment-only, per the independent source reviews. No line that is not a // comment
changed; the five production behaviours and every control body are byte-identical
to PATCH 5 (66abf383842, tree 30be39d4d0af).

N1 (src/v2/test/claim/cli/population_verbs.dag): the new control's header predicted
that deleting the standing demotion would show "reused=1, parsed=1 and a receipt".
Wrong. The member then takes the Reused arm, which reaches population_parse_accepted
as well, so its roster arm refuses the declared key either way: parsed stays 0 and
no receipt appears. What changes is reused becomes 1 and miss_declared_refused stays
0, which reddens the control on those two conjuncts.

N2 (same file): the receipt line was quoted as "sha256:<digest> <compiler>". The
speller is gunbc.parse_verdict_schema.parse_verdict_stored_accepted_line, which
emits "parse-verdict" TAB source_digest TAB compiler TAB "Accepted";
parse_verdict_receipt_lines keys its Map by the folded line, so the artifact carries
no member identity at all and the key-swap mutation is not expressible here. The
UNOBSERVABLE relabelling stands on that stronger reason.

N3 (src/v2/cli/population_verbs.dag, production header of
population_parse_member_decided): it still credited walk_population_controls with
running parse-population "over the repository". It holds check-layout over the live
roots and walks the verb over the FIXTURE roots only; the repository walk runs in the
gate's parse-verdict steps, and the Reused arm of a publish runs only once
witnesses.yml carries --reuse-from. No sentence claims the new route has run.

Nothing executed: no CI job runs witnesses or v1 unit tests, so every RED/GREEN
statement remains a prediction from a source reading.
